{title: All Hail the Power of Jesus' Name}
{lyricist: Edward Perronet}
{composer: Oliver Holden}
{year: 1779}
{meta: tune-year 1793}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune CORONATION}
{meta: meter CM (8.6.8.6) with repeat}
{meta: variation The hymn, sung to CORONATION}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: note Altered by John Rippon in 1787.}
{meta: tags praise, Christ the King}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
All [G]hail the [C]power of [G]Jesus' [D]name!
Let [G]angels [D]prostrate [G]fall;
Bring [G]forth the [C]royal [G]di[D]a[G]dem,
And [C]crown [G]Him Lord of [D]all;
Bring [G]forth the [C]royal [G]di[D]a[G]dem,
And [C]crown [G]Him [D]Lord of [G]all.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Ye [G]chosen [C]seed of [G]Israel's [D]race,
Ye [G]ransomed [D]from the [G]fall,
Hail [G]Him who [C]saves you [G]by [D]His [G]grace,
And [C]crown [G]Him Lord of [D]all;
Hail [G]Him who [C]saves you [G]by [D]His [G]grace,
And [C]crown [G]Him [D]Lord of [G]all.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Let [G]every [C]kindred, [G]every [D]tribe,
On [G]this ter[D]restrial [G]ball,
To [G]Him all [C]majes[G]ty [D]as[G]cribe,
And [C]crown [G]Him Lord of [D]all;
To [G]Him all [C]majes[G]ty [D]as[G]cribe,
And [C]crown [G]Him [D]Lord of [G]all.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
O [G]that with [C]yonder [G]sacred [D]throng
We [G]at His [D]feet may [G]fall!
We'll [G]join the [C]ever[G]last[D]ing [G]song,
And [C]crown [G]Him Lord of [D]all;
We'll [G]join the [C]ever[G]last[D]ing [G]song,
And [C]crown [G]Him [D]Lord of [G]all.
{end_of_verse}
